  "_comment": [
    "NBA arenas since 2000: the 30 current home arenas, every former home arena in the range, and the neutral, international and preseason venues ESPN lists five or more games at.",
    "Coordinates are from OpenStreetMap Nominatim (coords_source nominatim, queried 2026-09-18) or the Wikipedia infobox where Nominatim could not place the building.",
    "provider_ids.espn_venue_ids are the ids ESPN's scoreboard gives the building (docs/verification.md); the CDN schedule names arenas, which resolve through aliases.",
    "home_by_season fills the venue of a historical game ESPN has no venue for (Reunion Arena, Compaq Center, the Pyramid, GM Place): the home team's arena in that season, by the team abbreviation in seed/nba_teams.json.",
    "The Alamodome, which the Spurs used through 2001-02, is the NFL seed's row; the migration adds nba to its sports and its ESPN id.",
    "geofence_m is 250: an arena is a smaller building than a stadium."
